    },
    "message": "Move the per-tick KPI columns and entity rules to Rust\n\nMetricSnapshot.from_world and operational_kpi_values read the rows in one\ncall each (rules/metrics.rs). The entity and event rules of validate at the\nend of a tick are one kernel that reads the objects and answers yes or\nUnsupported (rules/tick_validation.rs), so the Python rules and their error\ntexts stay, split into _validate_entity_rules and _validate_event_rules.\npopulation_dynamics_v1 with no one pending has a kernel too. The zone\nenvironment config is read again only when it or the zones change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
